<h1 class="text-4xl pb-4 border-b border-dashed border-terminal-dim">World Structure</h1>

<p class="text-2xl pt-6 pb-4">
  The world data is a single JSON object with five top-level keys. This is the root document that defines your entire game.
</p>

<h2 id="schema" class="doc-section text-3xl pt-6 pb-3 border-b border-terminal-dim">Schema</h2>

<pre class="doc-code text-terminal-green mt-4">{
  <span class="key">"meta"</span>: {
    <span class="key">"name"</span>: <span class="str">"My Adventure"</span>,        <span class="comment">// Required - human-readable game name</span>
    <span class="key">"description"</span>: <span class="str">"A short quest..."</span>, <span class="comment">// Required - game description</span>
    <span class="key">"starting_room"</span>: <span class="str">"room_id"</span>,   <span class="comment">// Required - where the player begins</span>
    <span class="key">"version"</span>: <span class="str">"1.0"</span>              <span class="comment">// Optional - version identifier</span>
  },
  <span class="key">"rooms"</span>: {
    <span class="str">"room_id"</span>: { <span class="comment">/* room definition */</span> }
  },
  <span class="key">"items"</span>: {
    <span class="str">"item_id"</span>: { <span class="comment">/* item definition */</span> }
  },
  <span class="key">"npcs"</span>: {
    <span class="str">"npc_id"</span>: { <span class="comment">/* NPC definition */</span> }
  },
  <span class="key">"creatures"</span>: {
    <span class="str">"creature_id"</span>: { <span class="comment">/* creature definition */</span> }
  }
}</pre>

<h2 id="meta" class="doc-section text-3xl pt-8 pb-3 border-b border-terminal-dim">meta</h2>

<p class="text-xl pt-4 pb-3">Controls game-wide configuration.</p>

<table class="doc-table">
  <thead>
    <tr><th>Field</th><th>Type</th><th>Required</th><th>Description</th></tr>
  </thead>
  <tbody>
    <tr>
      <td><code>name</code></td>
      <td>string</td>
      <td><span class="badge badge-required">required</span></td>
      <td>Human-readable name for the game, displayed to players.</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><code>description</code></td>
      <td>string</td>
      <td><span class="badge badge-required">required</span></td>
      <td>A short description of the game or its premise.</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><code>starting_room</code></td>
      <td>string</td>
      <td><span class="badge badge-required">required</span></td>
      <td>The room ID where the player begins. Must match a key in <code>rooms</code>.</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><code>version</code></td>
      <td>string</td>
      <td><span class="badge badge-optional">optional</span></td>
      <td>Version identifier for your game world.</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><code>author</code></td>
      <td>string</td>
      <td><span class="badge badge-optional">optional</span></td>
      <td>Who wrote the world. Informational only.</td>
    </tr>
  </tbody>
</table>

<h2 id="rooms" class="doc-section text-3xl pt-8 pb-3 border-b border-terminal-dim">rooms</h2>

<p class="text-xl pt-4 pb-3">
  An object where each key is a unique room ID and each value is a <a href="/docs/rooms" class="text-terminal-bright hover:underline">Room definition</a>. Room IDs are used throughout the world data to reference locations.
</p>

<pre class="doc-code text-terminal-green mt-2"><span class="key">"rooms"</span>: {
  <span class="key">"tavern"</span>: { <span class="comment">/* ... */</span> },
  <span class="key">"cellar"</span>: { <span class="comment">/* ... */</span> },
  <span class="key">"forest_clearing"</span>: { <span class="comment">/* ... */</span> }
}</pre>

<h2 id="items" class="doc-section text-3xl pt-8 pb-3 border-b border-terminal-dim">items</h2>

<p class="text-xl pt-4 pb-3">
  An object where each key is a unique item ID and each value is an <a href="/docs/items" class="text-terminal-bright hover:underline">Item definition</a>. Items are placed by listing their IDs in a room's <code>items</code> array. See <a href="#room-state" class="text-terminal-bright hover:underline">Placing Entities in Rooms</a>.
</p>

<pre class="doc-code text-terminal-green mt-2"><span class="key">"items"</span>: {
  <span class="key">"rusty_sword"</span>: { <span class="comment">/* ... */</span> },
  <span class="key">"health_potion"</span>: { <span class="comment">/* ... */</span> },
  <span class="key">"wooden_chest"</span>: { <span class="comment">/* ... */</span> }
}</pre>

<h2 id="npcs" class="doc-section text-3xl pt-8 pb-3 border-b border-terminal-dim">npcs</h2>

<p class="text-xl pt-4 pb-3">
  An object where each key is a unique NPC ID and each value is an <a href="/docs/npcs" class="text-terminal-bright hover:underline">NPC definition</a>. NPCs are placed by listing their IDs in a room's <code>npcs</code> array. See <a href="#room-state" class="text-terminal-bright hover:underline">Placing Entities in Rooms</a>.
</p>

<pre class="doc-code text-terminal-green mt-2"><span class="key">"npcs"</span>: {
  <span class="key">"bartender"</span>: { <span class="comment">/* ... */</span> },
  <span class="key">"mysterious_wizard"</span>: { <span class="comment">/* ... */</span> }
}</pre>

<h2 id="creatures" class="doc-section text-3xl pt-8 pb-3 border-b border-terminal-dim">creatures</h2>

<p class="text-xl pt-4 pb-3">
  An object where each key is a unique creature ID and each value is a <a href="/docs/creatures" class="text-terminal-bright hover:underline">Creature definition</a>. Creatures are placed by listing their IDs in a room's <code>creatures</code> array (see <a href="#room-state" class="text-terminal-bright hover:underline">Placing Entities in Rooms</a>) and can be attacked to initiate <a href="/docs/combat#starting" class="text-terminal-bright hover:underline">combat</a>.
</p>

<pre class="doc-code text-terminal-green mt-2"><span class="key">"creatures"</span>: {
  <span class="key">"goblin"</span>: { <span class="comment">/* ... */</span> },
  <span class="key">"dragon"</span>: { <span class="comment">/* ... */</span> }
}</pre>

<h2 id="ids" class="doc-section text-3xl pt-8 pb-3 border-b border-terminal-dim">About IDs</h2>

<p class="text-xl pt-4 pb-3">
  All IDs (room, item, NPC, creature) are strings you define. They are used internally to reference entities across the world data. Recommendations:
</p>

<ul class="text-xl list-disc list-inside space-y-2 pt-2">
  <li>Use lowercase with underscores: <code class="text-terminal-bright">old_sword</code>, <code class="text-terminal-bright">dark_forest</code></li>
  <li>Keep them descriptive but concise</li>
  <li>IDs must be unique within their category (rooms, items, npcs, creatures)</li>
  <li>IDs are never shown to the player - they only see <code>name</code> fields</li>
</ul>

<h2 id="room-state" class="doc-section text-3xl pt-8 pb-3 border-b border-terminal-dim">Placing Entities in Rooms</h2>

<p class="text-xl pt-4 pb-3">
  Items, NPCs, and creatures are placed by listing their IDs on the room itself. Every room definition accepts three optional arrays:
</p>

<pre class="doc-code text-terminal-green mt-2"><span class="key">"tavern"</span>: {
  <span class="key">"name"</span>: <span class="str">"The Tavern"</span>,
  <span class="key">"description"</span>: <span class="str">"A dimly lit tavern with a roaring fireplace..."</span>,
  <span class="key">"exits"</span>: { <span class="key">"north"</span>: <span class="str">"town_square"</span> },
  <span class="key">"items"</span>: [<span class="str">"rusty_sword"</span>, <span class="str">"health_potion"</span>],
  <span class="key">"npcs"</span>: [<span class="str">"bartender"</span>],
  <span class="key">"creatures"</span>: [<span class="str">"goblin"</span>]
}</pre>

<p class="text-xl pt-4 pb-3">
  When a game starts, the engine copies these arrays into each room's <a href="/docs/flags-and-state#room-state" class="text-terminal-bright hover:underline">room state</a>, which then changes as players take items and defeat creatures. Your world definition is never modified. Items that only ever come out of a <a href="/docs/containers" class="text-terminal-bright hover:underline">container</a>, a creature's <a href="/docs/creatures#loot" class="text-terminal-bright hover:underline">loot</a>, or an NPC's <code>gives_item</code> do not need to be listed in any room.
</p>
